# SECURITY: prevent secrets and operator-supplied configuration from being
# baked into image layers. The Dockerfile uses `COPY . /usr/local/node/trinket`,
# which copies the entire repository unless filtered here. Without these
# exclusions, an operator who builds the image with a real `config/local.yaml`
# (containing the session cookie password and other secrets) would leak those
# secrets into image layers, recoverable via `docker history` or by anyone
# who pulls the image. QA finding #7.

# Source-control metadata
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# SECURITY: local / environment-specific configuration that contains secrets
# (session cookie password, JWT signing keys, OAuth client secrets, SMTP
# credentials, etc.). The image must rely on operator-supplied configuration
# at runtime via volume mounts or environment variables, never via files
# baked into the image.
config/local.yaml
config/local.yml
config/local.json
config/development.yaml
config/development.yml
config/development.json
config/production.yaml
config/production.yml
config/production.json
config/runtime.json
config/runtime.json.tmp-*
config/migration.json
config/migrationDb.json

# Installed dependencies (the Dockerfile runs `npm install` and downloads
# `public-components.tgz` inside the image, so these would be overwritten
# anyway; excluding speeds up the build context transfer).
node_modules
**/node_modules
public/components
public/vendor

# Generated migration backups (operator data, not part of image)
lib/migrations/backups

# IDE / editor metadata
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.idea
.vscode
*.swp

# Vagrant
Vagrantfile
.vagrant

# Logs and debug
npm-debug.log
build.log
test-*.js

# OS metadata
*.DS_Store

# Compiled Python
*.pyc

# Blitzy / agent working directory (build artifacts, screenshots, reports)
blitzy

# Test ad-hoc files
blitzy_adhoc_test_*

# SCSS source maps and cache (CSS files in public/css/ are kept — they are
# built locally by `npm run build` and must be present in the image because
# the Dockerfile does not run the SCSS build step)
.sass-cache
